Draw NextUI's and rgds-core's screen shaders on the CPU: the Visual FX
page's SHADER PRESET row and a Shaders page behind it with COLOUR, SCALING,
FILTER, PATTERN, GLOW and CURVE, and hotkeys that step COLOUR, PATTERN and
the preset.

rgds-core runs its shaders as GLES2 fragment programs by hooking
SDL_RenderCopy, and NextUI's minarch as GLES passes. The pak's devices draw
through fbdev or the Allwinner display engine, where there is no GL stage,
so each is done here: colours and filters at DS resolution, a resampler in
place of the nearest scaler, patterns over the scaler's rows (or as the
display engine's overlay layer), and the barrel curve over the finished
views.

The maths, the tables and the NEON kernels live in minui_shader.{h,cpp},
minui_resample.{h,cpp} and the row names and presets in
minui_shader_presets.h, vendored in overlay/ in the pak repo and copied into
the tree by the Makefile before this patch is applied, so nothing here adds
a file. The patch applies after 0003 and builds on a few of its lines: the
game_switcher action in input.{h,cpp}, fade_out and the hotkey notice in
main.cpp.

What it changes:

  gpu.{h,cpp}         Gpu::ScaleTarget gains, at its end, a colour table and
                      function, run on each line before anything else in
                      emit_scaled; a line filter that holds lines back (the
                      glow's blur and FILTER need the lines below), with the
                      rest of emit_scaled moved to emit_line; a resampler
                      that takes the scaler's place; and a pattern's class
                      rows, bright rows for the spread, and their kernel, run
                      on the plain nearest path. All null by default, so an
                      upstream build scales exactly as before. fb_ is never
                      written: screenshots, thumbnails and states keep the
                      game's own colours.
  display.{h,cpp}     set_shaders(): the resampler and the pattern's rows per
                      view in build_scale, rebuilt live as a layout change
                      rebuilds the x-maps; under a curve, every view scaled
                      into its side buffer and curved into the frame by
                      finish_views, the pattern drawn after it.
  display_disp.{h,cpp}  the patterns that only darken, drawn as the overlay
                      layer's image in place of the LCD grid.
  settings.{h,cpp}    SHADER PRESET after BILINEAR, and kShaderSettings, the
                      Shaders page's table; Dep::Scaling, Pattern, Glow and
                      Bloom.
  main.cpp            video.preset, colour, scaling, filter, pattern, glow and
                      curve, an unknown name being off with a warning; the
                      colour table, built on its own thread and committed
                      between frames, applied in the scaler and to the frames
                      the tiers without one take whole, the pause menu's
                      backdrop and the quit fade; the resampler and pattern
                      handed to the scaler, over bilinear, chunky, the grid
                      and seams as each allows; the filters per screen, auto
                      glow being crt's halation; why a row is off; a preset
                      setting the rows and a row edit making it custom; and
                      colour_next, colour_prev, pattern_next, pattern_prev,
                      preset_next and preset_prev, which step a row as the
                      page does, say so in the notice and keep it for the
                      game.
  input.{h,cpp}       the six actions, unbound by default.
  config.cpp, default.ini  document the keys.
  CMakeLists          build minui_shader.cpp and minui_resample.cpp into
                      dsperate; register test_minui_shader.

menu.h and menu.cpp are untouched: the rows come from the settings tables.
